.env
# A copy of .env under any other name (`.env.bak`, `.env.local`, `.env.old`) is still a
# copy of every key in it: `.env` alone matched nothing else, and a `git add -A` would
# have committed a live NIM and JEV key. `.env.example` stays tracked on purpose.
.env*
!.env.example

